                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "HOW TO SURVIVE 2: AN ABSOLUTE DISGRACE, A COMPLETE WASTE OF TIME AND MONEY\r\n\r\nLet me make one thing clear: HOW TO SURVIVE 2 is quite simply the worst game I have ever played in my entire life. It's an absolute disaster, a frustrating experience from beginning to end, and an insult to everyone who enjoyed the first game. I genuinely don't understand how anyone could release a game in this state and expect players to actually enjoy it.\r\n\r\nLet's start with the bugs. This game is so poorly made that some achievements are simply unobtainable because of bugs. Yes, achievements you can spend hours trying to unlock, only to eventually realize that the problem isn't you, but the game itself. I find this absolutely outrageous, especially for players like me who enjoy completing games 100%. It's a complete nightmare. We're not talking about difficulty, challenge, or skill anymore; we're talking about a game that prevents you from making proper progress because it's fundamentally broken.\r\n\r\nBut the worst part is that the bugs aren't even the only problem. The game is poorly designed, frustrating, and constantly feels like it was rushed and half-assed. The mechanics, progression, and overall experience make you want to throw your controller against a wall. Instead of making you want to keep playing, every session becomes a test of patience. You spend your time replaying quests because of bugs and other issues instead of simply being able to enjoy the game. It's absolutely ridiculous.\r\n\r\nI'm not even going to waste too much time discussing how every mission eventually starts feeling the same, making progression repetitive and incredibly boring. As for the weapons, they all look pretty much identical visually. The only real differences are the stats and numbers. There's no real sense of novelty, no distinctive visual identity, and nothing that genuinely makes you excited to discover the next piece of equipment. Overall, it feels like the developers took the easiest route at every opportunity instead of putting any real effort into expanding their ideas or making the experience genuinely engaging. This lack of ambition and variety is downright infuriating, especially in a game that relies so heavily on progression and repeating activities.\r\n\r\nAnd the most frustrating part of all this is that the first HOW TO SURVIVE was far more enjoyable. Instead of taking what made the original good and intelligently building upon it, this sequel feels like a much worse version of a formula that already worked. Where the first game had its charm, this one piles up flaws until it completely wears down the player's patience. It's a massive waste of potential: a sequel that should have been better, but instead manages to make you want to go back and play its predecessor.\r\n\r\nUltimately, HOW TO SURVIVE 2 is a monumental waste of time and money. You buy a game to have fun, not to fight against bugs, get stuck in your progression, and waste hours trying to unlock achievements that the game itself seems incapable of registering. I'll never get back the time I wasted on this game, and that's probably what pisses me off the most.\r\n\r\nMy verdict: stay the hell away from this disaster. If you want to discover the series, play the first HOW TO SURVIVE, which is infinitely better in my opinion. As for HOW TO SURVIVE 2, I consider it a failed sequel: poorly designed, riddled with bugs, painfully repetitive, and completely unworthy of the time and attention you might give it.\r\n\r\nI absolutely cannot recommend this game. Between the bugs, unobtainable achievements, repetitive missions, lack of variety, and the constant feeling that the whole thing was half-assed, HOW TO SURVIVE 2 is a massive disappointment. A game that turns entertainment into a chore, a purchase I regret, and a sequel that can't even do justice to the original.",
